WEBVTT

1
00:01:16.664 --> 00:01:20.134
Well, it was here... someplace.

2
00:01:20.168 --> 00:01:23.271
But we've already been past here.

3
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.276
The trees have grown so big.

4
00:01:30.178 --> 00:01:33.214
It's been so long
since my last visit.

5
00:01:40.355 --> 00:01:42.724
Come on. Blaze.

6
00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:46.394
Grandma, when was
the last time you were here?

7
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.963
Years and years ago.

8
00:01:48.997 --> 00:01:52.734
Way before you were born, sweetheart.

9
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.504
Oh, look! Blaze found a squirrel.

10
00:01:56.537 --> 00:02:00.808
Now, just a minute.
I'm trying to get my bearings.

11
00:02:00.842 --> 00:02:03.711
Oh, there are so many paths here.

12
00:02:03.745 --> 00:02:07.248
So easy to get turned around.
Come on, darling.

13
00:02:07.315 --> 00:02:10.785
Grandma,
we're in the middle of nowhere!

14
00:02:10.852 --> 00:02:13.821
We're right in the middle
of New York City!

15
00:02:13.855 --> 00:02:16.758
You'll make yourself tired
walking so long.

16
00:02:16.858 --> 00:02:20.728
Nonsense. It hasn't been
more than a quarter of an hour.

17
00:02:21.863 --> 00:02:23.331
Not much further.

18
00:02:23.364 --> 00:02:25.333
Blaze is getting tired.

19
00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:27.235
Oh, I see!

20
00:02:30.238 --> 00:02:33.241
Grandma,
what are we looking for anyway?

21
00:02:33.274 --> 00:02:35.276
Uh, a memorial.

22
00:02:35.343 --> 00:02:37.779
A me... - what?

23
00:02:37.845 --> 00:02:41.749
A reminder of a wonderful story...

24
00:02:41.816 --> 00:02:45.019
and a place very far away from here.

25
00:02:45.053 --> 00:02:47.088
What place is that. Grandma?

26
00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.359
Nome, Alaska.

27
00:02:51.392 --> 00:02:55.063
It's a small town
almost on top of the world.

28
00:02:55.096 --> 00:02:56.698
Hmm.

29
00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.268
Now, that really was
in the middle of nowhere, sweetheart.

30
00:03:01.736 --> 00:03:06.641
In the cold winter of 1925,

31
00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.210
it was snowing hard.

32
00:03:11.279 --> 00:03:15.550
<i>Back then, the fastest and most
reliable way of getting around</i>

33
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:19.554
<i>was with teams of dogs
pulling long sleds.</i>

34
00:03:19.587 --> 00:03:24.659
<i>Races were held every year
to find out the best team.</i>

35
00:03:26.327 --> 00:03:29.931
<i>And the competition
was very fierce.</i>

36
00:03:33.668 --> 00:03:35.770
Mush!

37
00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.812
Gee up, boy.

38
00:03:49.317 --> 00:03:52.153
Giddap, Steele! Giddap, giddap!

39
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.337
Steele! Whoa! Whoa!

40
00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.609
Steele, we're not gonna make it!

41
00:04:17.245 --> 00:04:21.916
- Easy, now! Easy!
- Steele, hold back!

42
00:04:36.698 --> 00:04:38.900
Ohh! Steele!

43
00:04:38.966 --> 00:04:41.502
Get in line, Steele!

44
00:04:41.569 --> 00:04:43.338
Get in line!

45
00:04:45.306 --> 00:04:48.409
Mush! Mush!

46
00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.314
It's the three-mile marker.

47
00:04:53.348 --> 00:04:57.285
Balto,
get your slobbering mouth off me!

48
00:04:57.318 --> 00:05:00.488
Let's go, Boris. We'll get around back
and catch the end of the race.

49
00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.392
Oh, no. No, no, no.
I'm a delicate country bird.

50
00:05:05.626 --> 00:05:07.695
I hate going into town.

51
00:05:07.729 --> 00:05:11.265
Ah, come on.
What's the worst that can happen?

52
00:05:16.337 --> 00:05:18.873
Please! Aah!

53
00:05:20.208 --> 00:05:22.877
Why do I let you talk me
into these things?

54
00:05:33.788 --> 00:05:36.858
What the... ?! Eeeh!

55
00:05:48.336 --> 00:05:51.372
Bring that back, you thief!

56
00:05:54.876 --> 00:06:01.282
- You are putting me down now, Mr Golden Retriever?
- Whatever you say, Boris.

57
00:06:01.315 --> 00:06:04.952
Every time there's a race,
you run around like you're in it.

58
00:06:05.053 --> 00:06:07.488
- Maybe one day I will be.
- Heel, boy!

59
00:06:07.555 --> 00:06:10.324
Boris Goosinoff is no spring chicken.

60
00:06:14.429 --> 00:06:16.998
I'm no spring penguin, either!

61
00:06:17.065 --> 00:06:20.134
Oy, it's cold!

62
00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.206
Look! The two-mile mark.

63
00:06:25.239 --> 00:06:27.442
Come on! We don't wanna miss the finish.

64
00:06:27.508 --> 00:06:29.477
Oh, that would be a tragedy.

65
00:06:31.446 --> 00:06:33.681
I was being sarcastic.

66
00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.120
OK, you can open your eyes now.

67
00:06:44.859 --> 00:06:48.596
I love these runners!
I love this brush bow!

68
00:06:48.629 --> 00:06:51.632
I love this sled!
Jenna, you're lead dog!

69
00:06:51.666 --> 00:06:54.769
OK, just a minute. Come on. Mush!

70
00:06:54.802 --> 00:06:56.871
Then you'll need... this.

71
00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:01.109
A real musher's hat!
We're a real sled team now!

72
00:07:01.109 --> 00:07:02.343
Mush!

73
00:07:02.377 --> 00:07:05.313
Mister Johanssen,
the sled is beautiful.

74
00:07:05.346 --> 00:07:08.149
- We're very grateful.
- Oh, thank you!

75
00:07:08.182 --> 00:07:11.085
- Rosy's grateful too, huh?
- So I gather!

76
00:07:11.152 --> 00:07:13.788
- Watch this!
- Coming, sweetheart.

77
00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.858
I don't know, honey, maybe we
should've gotten her the doll house!

78
00:07:17.458 --> 00:07:19.560
It's the one-mile marker.

79
00:07:19.627 --> 00:07:22.697
Mush, Jenna, mush!
Let's win this race!

80
00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:26.167
I think she'll learn to like it!

81
00:07:27.669 --> 00:07:30.004
Jenna. Easy, girl.

82
00:07:31.906 --> 00:07:36.878
Good morning, Jenna. Oughta be
a close race, don't you think?

83
00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:39.814
Maybe even neck and... neck.

84
00:07:39.847 --> 00:07:44.652
Say something about her new collar
before she gets whiplash.

85
00:07:44.686 --> 00:07:47.455
Urn, Dixie, what a pretty collar.
Is it new?

86
00:07:47.488 --> 00:07:49.324
What? This old thing?

87
00:07:49.357 --> 00:07:53.528
Yeah. Do you think,
urn, Steele will notice?

88
00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.765
I'm afraid the only way Steele notices
anyone is if they're wearing a mirror.

89
00:07:57.832 --> 00:07:59.934
They're comin'!

90
00:08:07.408 --> 00:08:10.645
- Steele!
- You can do it!

91
00:08:10.678 --> 00:08:12.780
Jenna! Stay, girl!

92
00:08:12.847 --> 00:08:14.882
That's some dog!

93
00:08:22.423 --> 00:08:24.225
Jenna!

94
00:08:28.496 --> 00:08:31.766
Hold on. Come on, Steele!

95
00:08:31.799 --> 00:08:33.768
Oh, no!

96
00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.245
My hat!

97
00:08:54.922 --> 00:08:58.426
- It's that stray dog!
- He's gonna ruin the race!

98
00:09:02.897 --> 00:09:05.833
Hey! Outta my way, lobo.

99
00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:26.821
When will you learn
to stay on the sidelines?

100
00:09:35.296 --> 00:09:37.799
To Juneau Daily Chronicle. Stop.

101
00:09:37.832 --> 00:09:40.768
Steele wins first race
of season. Stop.

102
00:09:40.835 --> 00:09:45.039
Three-time winner keeps
Golden Collar. Stop. Nome. Stop.

103
00:09:45.106 --> 00:09:48.276
That Steele is some dog, huh, Morris?

104
00:09:51.312 --> 00:09:53.981
Congratulations there, boss, there.

105
00:09:54.048 --> 00:09:56.651
It was a pleasure
runnin' behind youse.

106
00:09:56.684 --> 00:09:58.686
Of course, the view got monotonous.

107
00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:02.290
You are the most amazing, the most exalted,
the most pre-eminent, the most top of...

108
00:10:02.323 --> 00:10:03.958
You won!

109
00:10:07.729 --> 00:10:11.199
I don't know.
You think maybe Steele is losing his edge?

110
00:10:11.265 --> 00:10:14.202
Yeah, looks like just about any dog
could outrun him.

111
00:10:17.538 --> 00:10:22.210
What a crazy thing to do
just to show off to a pretty girl!

112
00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:26.748
I'm sure Jenna would love
to have you on her team.

113
00:10:26.814 --> 00:10:29.484
- Hey! Rosy! Stay away from him!
- Dad!

114
00:10:29.517 --> 00:10:32.854
He might bite you, honey.
He's part wolf.

115
00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.656
Now you've hurt his feelings.

116
00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.493
Come on now.

117
00:10:38.526 --> 00:10:41.162
Congratulations, Steele.

118
00:10:41.195 --> 00:10:43.531
Ladies.

119
00:10:46.067 --> 00:10:48.936
- Hi, there, Jenna. Enjoy the race?
- Yeah.

120
00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.939
- Almost as much as you did.
- Thanks.

121
00:10:52.006 --> 00:10:55.743
Jenna, let's go celebrate. I know
where all the bones are buried.

122
00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:59.380
I don't know.
Suddenly, I've lost my appetite.

123
00:11:01.516 --> 00:11:06.554
Well, maybe your taste
runs more toward... wolf.

124
00:11:06.587 --> 00:11:09.724
Jenna! Come on, girl.
We're going back home.

125
00:11:09.757 --> 00:11:12.593
Sorry, Steele.
My girl is calling me.

126
00:11:12.627 --> 00:11:15.096
On the other hand.

127
00:11:15.129 --> 00:11:18.633
my girl is away
at boarding school.

128
00:11:34.115 --> 00:11:39.153
Jenna!

129
00:11:45.493 --> 00:11:48.763
Jenna, I, uh...

130
00:11:48.896 --> 00:11:51.566
- Jenna.
- Jen! Come on!

131
00:12:00.975 --> 00:12:03.611
Jenna! Come here, girl.

132
00:12:06.647 --> 00:12:10.518
Balto, there's some things
I can't do for you.

133
00:12:10.585 --> 00:12:11.986
Yeah.

134
00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:13.955
I'm goose, not Cupid.

135
00:12:13.988 --> 00:12:16.457
Didn't make the team... Bingo?

136
00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:19.327
Don't listen to him or look at him.
Live a long life.

137
00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.329
My name's Balto.

138
00:12:21.396 --> 00:12:23.531
But you can call him "idiot"!

139
00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.067
I'm sorry. Balto.
Balto the half-breed.

140
00:12:27.702 --> 00:12:30.104
Hey, goose,
you a half-breed too, huh?

141
00:12:30.138 --> 00:12:33.174
- Part turkey?
- Waa-hah-hah!

142
00:12:33.207 --> 00:12:35.009
Good wordplay there, boss.

143
00:12:35.076 --> 00:12:37.178
You are the wittiest, the quickest.

144
00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:41.149
You are the drollest, the cleverest,
the sharpest, the most hilarious...

145
00:12:41.182 --> 00:12:43.017
You crack me up!

146
00:12:48.056 --> 00:12:50.925
Steele. Just leave him out of this.

147
00:12:50.992 --> 00:12:55.229
Oh, Balto, I've got a message
for your mother.

148
00:13:01.703 --> 00:13:03.705
Hi, Mom!

149
00:13:03.738 --> 00:13:07.408
Balto, translate this for me...

150
00:13:07.475 --> 00:13:09.911
What's wolf for "Go chase your tail"?

151
00:13:09.944 --> 00:13:11.446
Balto, stop! Whoa!

152
00:13:16.284 --> 00:13:18.353
Get him.

153
00:13:19.887 --> 00:13:23.458
Get out of here, wolf-dog.
You'd better get back to your pack!

154
00:13:23.558 --> 00:13:28.496
Maybe it's the unrelenting fear talking,
but I'm seeing wisdom in this advice.

155
00:13:28.563 --> 00:13:30.465
Maybe we go now, huh? Now!

156
00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:35.570
I'm thinking Balto's friend
got his feathers ruffled!

157
00:13:35.603 --> 00:13:37.538
Goose! Ha! I get it!

158
00:13:40.942 --> 00:13:43.745
Half-wolf in the side pocket there.

159
00:13:43.778 --> 00:13:47.782
That was the most dead centre,
the most on-target, the most down-the-middle...

160
00:13:47.815 --> 00:13:49.751
Ya hit him!

161
00:13:56.324 --> 00:13:58.159
That son-of-a...

162
00:13:58.226 --> 00:14:02.997
He is the most malicious, the most disgusting,
obnoxious, the most revolting, the most repulsive...

163
00:14:03.064 --> 00:14:04.766
He's no lap dog.

164
00:14:42.804 --> 00:14:45.940
Not a dog, not a wolf.

165
00:14:46.007 --> 00:14:49.610
All he knows is what he is not.

166
00:14:49.644 --> 00:14:52.980
If only he could see what he is.

167
00:16:02.517 --> 00:16:04.986
Homesick, Boris?

168
00:16:05.019 --> 00:16:09.090
- You ever think about going back?
- Don't fret, Fido.

169
00:16:09.157 --> 00:16:12.894
I'm sticking here until I'm sure
you can stand on own four feet.

170
00:16:12.927 --> 00:16:16.364
- YOU'RE taking care of ME?!
- Don't thank me.

171
00:16:17.799 --> 00:16:20.234
I smell... herring.

172
00:16:20.268 --> 00:16:23.604
- The herring are flying south too?
- Say!

173
00:16:23.638 --> 00:16:26.474
- Must be Muk and Luk.
- Oh. Good news.

174
00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.777
- Uncle Boris!
- Oh, no!

175
00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:32.814
How sweet. "Uncle Boris. "

176
00:16:32.914 --> 00:16:34.749
No hugging, no licking!

177
00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.920
Uncle Boris!

178
00:16:46.427 --> 00:16:50.164
He says he's glad to see you.

179
00:16:50.298 --> 00:16:52.066
We love you. Uncle Boris.

180
00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:15.323
What are you talking about?
Of course he's glad to see us.

181
00:17:15.356 --> 00:17:19.160
He loves us... don't you?

182
00:17:19.193 --> 00:17:21.462
Oy. OK, ОК.

183
00:17:21.496 --> 00:17:25.166
Hey, boychicks, uh, let's play a game.

184
00:17:25.199 --> 00:17:27.001
Yes, please. Uncle Boris.

185
00:17:27.035 --> 00:17:29.337
Race you to the shore.
One, two, three, go!

186
00:17:31.339 --> 00:17:33.341
They win.

187
00:17:33.374 --> 00:17:36.544
Help! Help! We can't swim!

188
00:17:38.012 --> 00:17:41.482
Help! Help! We're drowning!
Save us, please!

189
00:17:41.516 --> 00:17:42.884
Bears!

190
00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:47.655
- Fellas! Idiot balls of fluff!
- Easy, Boris. You know how they are.

191
00:17:47.689 --> 00:17:49.357
Muk! Luk!

192
00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:52.727
Relax! Come on, you're OK.
You're not drowning.

193
00:17:54.529 --> 00:17:57.965
He has point, bears.
You are not drowning.

194
00:17:57.999 --> 00:18:01.436
Cause if you will pause one moment
you will observe that's...

195
00:18:01.536 --> 00:18:03.471
... tide is out!

196
00:18:07.875 --> 00:18:09.877
He said what?

197
00:18:09.944 --> 00:18:13.815
Oh, the shame of the polar bear
who fears the water.

198
00:18:13.948 --> 00:18:18.186
No wonder we are shunned
by our fellow bear. Woe is us!

199
00:18:18.219 --> 00:18:21.356
It's what he said.
Kind of pathetic, really.

200
00:18:21.389 --> 00:18:24.892
What, more whimpering?

201
00:18:24.926 --> 00:18:29.564
Between you and Balto, it's like
Dostoevsky novel here. Lighten up.

202
00:18:35.436 --> 00:18:37.505
And what is so interesting?

203
00:18:38.773 --> 00:18:41.743
- Jenna.
- Is love.

204
00:18:41.776 --> 00:18:44.312
So go make move.

205
00:18:44.345 --> 00:18:50.018
When the angels' balalaikas
strum the sweet song of love, mambo!

206
00:18:50.084 --> 00:18:52.520
Nan. She's not my type.

207
00:18:52.653 --> 00:18:55.323
And why not?
This wolf business again?

208
00:18:55.356 --> 00:18:58.826
What's wrong with being half
and half, I'd like to know?

209
00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.262
Sometimes I wish lik crazy,
I was half eagle.

210
00:19:01.295 --> 00:19:02.497
Why?

211
00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.932
Better profile, for one thing. Hmm.

212
00:19:04.966 --> 00:19:07.235
And no one eats you, for another.

213
00:19:13.808 --> 00:19:16.377
Jenna?

214
00:19:17.812 --> 00:19:19.947
Jenna!

215
00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:22.850
Jenna! Hi, girl!

216
00:19:32.827 --> 00:19:36.898
Rosy! Rosy, come on. You're gonna
catch your death out here.

217
00:19:36.964 --> 00:19:40.168
- OK, Dad.
- Come on, the doctor's waiting.

218
00:20:23.678 --> 00:20:24.712
Jenna?

219
00:20:24.746 --> 00:20:27.415
Jenna.

220
00:20:27.448 --> 00:20:29.617
Balto. Hi.

221
00:20:29.684 --> 00:20:31.753
Hi.

222
00:20:31.786 --> 00:20:34.856
Look, uh...

223
00:20:34.889 --> 00:20:38.059
Just a shot in the dark,
but I was wondering if...

224
00:20:38.092 --> 00:20:43.398
I don't know, maybe you'd like to
go chase a few sticks by moonlight.

225
00:20:50.872 --> 00:20:52.440
Jenna?

226
00:20:52.507 --> 00:20:56.210
- Rosy's in there.
- In a hospital? Why?

227
00:20:57.145 --> 00:21:00.248
She feels warm
and she has a terrible cough.

228
00:21:03.584 --> 00:21:05.720
Balto, what's wrong with her?

229
00:21:05.753 --> 00:21:11.092
Uh, I'm not sure,
but I know how to find out. Come on.

230
00:21:13.494 --> 00:21:15.730
I have the keys to the city.

231
00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:23.838
After you.

232
00:21:25.573 --> 00:21:28.009
Balto!

233
00:21:28.076 --> 00:21:31.179
Big paws kinda run in my family.

234
00:21:31.245 --> 00:21:34.015
At least, uh, one side of my family.

235
00:21:36.984 --> 00:21:41.422
- Stay close.
- No problem there.

236
00:21:45.827 --> 00:21:48.629
It's so gloomy down here.

237
00:21:48.663 --> 00:21:50.698
Not that I'm scared or anything.

238
00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:56.804
Gloomy? You kiddin'? It's the
most beautiful spot in the world.

239
00:21:56.938 --> 00:22:00.174
Dogs travel for years
just to be right here.

240
00:22:00.208 --> 00:22:03.344
Here? I can't see why.

241
00:22:03.378 --> 00:22:07.682
That's cos you're looking
at the bowl half empty.

242
00:22:07.715 --> 00:22:11.185
See this? It's the polar ice caps.

243
00:22:11.219 --> 00:22:13.855
Balto, those are broken bottles.

244
00:22:13.888 --> 00:22:17.291
And they're not half empty,
they're all empty.

245
00:22:17.358 --> 00:22:19.961
- The sun.
- Oh, Balto...

246
00:22:19.994 --> 00:22:23.398
And... to the north...

247
00:22:26.534 --> 00:22:29.904
The northern lights!

248
00:22:32.707 --> 00:22:35.276
Oh, Balto, you're right.

249
00:22:35.309 --> 00:22:38.079
It's beautiful.

250
00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:41.616
Yeah.

251
00:22:41.683 --> 00:22:43.584
Beautiful.

252
00:22:50.692 --> 00:22:54.796
- Good night, Rosy.
- I'm so cold.

253
00:22:54.829 --> 00:22:59.500
I have another blanket for you here.
Stay warm and get some rest.

254
00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:08.176
Doctor, how is she?

255
00:23:08.209 --> 00:23:11.779
Exhausted from coughing.
Her fever's getting worse.

256
00:23:11.846 --> 00:23:14.949
Looks like diphtheria.

257
00:23:15.016 --> 00:23:18.486
She's the 18th case this week.

258
00:23:20.188 --> 00:23:24.125
And I'm out of antitoxin.

259
00:23:26.027 --> 00:23:28.029
Jenna. Jenna, I'm sorry.

260
00:23:28.062 --> 00:23:31.699
Jenna, I...
I didn't mean to upset you.

261
00:23:31.733 --> 00:23:35.470
- I shouldn't have taken you there.
- No, I'm glad you did.

262
00:23:37.739 --> 00:23:39.574
Steele.

263
00:23:41.075 --> 00:23:42.310
Well, well.

264
00:23:42.377 --> 00:23:46.481
What's wrong with this picture?
Jenna, join me for dinner.

265
00:23:46.547 --> 00:23:49.584
You start at one end,
I'll start at the other.

266
00:23:49.617 --> 00:23:52.754
When we get to the middle, well...

267
00:23:52.787 --> 00:23:55.256
- You tell me.
- All right, Steele.

268
00:23:55.289 --> 00:23:57.392
No, Balto.

269
00:24:01.462 --> 00:24:04.866
Gee, Steele...

270
00:24:04.899 --> 00:24:08.036
... I have to admit your offer
is very tempting.

271
00:24:08.069 --> 00:24:10.471
It is.

272
00:24:11.606 --> 00:24:15.176
But these days I prefer my meat... cooked.

273
00:24:17.979 --> 00:24:21.516
Come on, let's go!

274
00:24:23.450 --> 00:24:25.620
What's all the noise?

275
00:24:25.687 --> 00:24:29.357
- I think it's over here.
- Jenna, come on.

276
00:24:37.432 --> 00:24:39.701
Looks like Balto's found a way
to your meat locker.

277
00:24:39.834 --> 00:24:43.671
Good thing Steele was here.
Good boy Steele, you've earned these.

278
00:24:43.705 --> 00:24:47.842
Besides, I can't use 'em after
that wild animal's touched 'em.

279
00:24:47.875 --> 00:24:52.447
Go on, get out of here, you thief!
Come on, Jenna, let's go home.

280
00:24:59.954 --> 00:25:02.824
Anchorage. Stop.

281
00:25:02.857 --> 00:25:05.059
Repeat, urgent request.

282
00:25:05.126 --> 00:25:08.963
More diphtheria antitoxin. Stop.

283
00:25:08.997 --> 00:25:12.266
Nome in grave danger. Stop.

284
00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:15.069
Please help. Stop.

285
00:25:28.549 --> 00:25:32.086
<i>Nome, pack ice closing in.</i>

286
00:25:32.153 --> 00:25:36.557
<i>Cannot ship antitoxin by sea.</i>

287
00:25:36.590 --> 00:25:39.560
<i>Will try by air.</i>

288
00:25:46.234 --> 00:25:49.237
<i>Nome, storm at airport.</i>

289
00:25:49.270 --> 00:25:53.975
<i>Planes grounded until storm clears.</i>

290
00:25:54.042 --> 00:25:56.244
<i>Many regrets.</i>

291
00:25:56.344 --> 00:25:59.447
<i>From Juneau, Office of the Governor,</i>

292
00:25:59.514 --> 00:26:03.785
<i>we are shipping antitoxin by rail. Stop.</i>

293
00:26:03.850 --> 00:26:06.454
<i>Train line ends at town ofNenana. Stop.</i>

294
00:26:06.520 --> 00:26:09.157
<i>Select fastest dogs for sled team.</i>

295
00:26:09.190 --> 00:26:13.594
<i>To carry antitoxin from Nenana to Nome. Stop.</i>

296
00:26:13.628 --> 00:26:17.932
<i>God willing, train will make it through. Stop.</i>

297
00:26:19.867 --> 00:26:24.772
... to select the fastest dogs for
the sled team to fetch the antitoxin.

298
00:26:24.872 --> 00:26:27.942
the race is from...

299
00:26:31.879 --> 00:26:36.250
Just look at him.
He's gonna save the entire town.

300
00:26:36.284 --> 00:26:39.887
He's positively... magnesium!

301
00:26:39.920 --> 00:26:43.057
It's not exactly a one-dog show, Dixie.

302
00:26:43.090 --> 00:26:46.160
They're racing to see who's gonna
be on the dog sled team.

303
00:26:46.227 --> 00:26:49.597
What's with you, Jenna?
Steele's a genuine hero.

304
00:26:49.630 --> 00:26:51.966
But do you give him a sniff?

305
00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:55.837
That's because Jenna
is running with Balto.

306
00:26:55.903 --> 00:27:00.441
She was seen in the boiler room
the other night with Balto.

307
00:27:00.475 --> 00:27:03.811
They went in together
and they left together.

308
00:27:03.845 --> 00:27:06.848
I heard it all from
a very reliable source.

309
00:27:06.914 --> 00:27:08.850
And don't bother to deny it.

310
00:27:08.916 --> 00:27:11.019
Well, then I won't.

311
00:27:11.085 --> 00:27:14.055
Oh! I'm speechless.

312
00:27:14.088 --> 00:27:17.158
All mushers, get your dogs ready!

313
00:27:17.225 --> 00:27:20.528
- The race is about to begin!
- Wait! Balto!

314
00:27:20.595 --> 00:27:25.099
Racing is a spectator sport.
It requires very little preparation.

315
00:27:27.268 --> 00:27:29.971
You sit, you arrange refreshments.

316
00:27:30.004 --> 00:27:31.973
You like potato chip?

317
00:27:34.475 --> 00:27:37.378
I'm not watching the race,
I'm running it.

318
00:27:38.946 --> 00:27:42.650
- You said what?
- Hey look, I wanna help Rosy get better.

319
00:27:42.684 --> 00:27:44.852
I can get that medicine through.

320
00:27:44.886 --> 00:27:46.821
First... First...

321
00:27:46.854 --> 00:27:50.958
First of all get it through your had that they
wouldn't put you in a sled team

322
00:27:50.992 --> 00:27:55.029
even if you did win, which won't happen
and if it did, it wouldn't matter.

323
00:27:55.029 --> 00:27:59.067
Boris, did you ever think maybe you're
the reason the other geese fly south?

324
00:27:59.133 --> 00:28:02.136
If only your feet
were as fast as your mouth.

325
00:28:02.170 --> 00:28:05.006
- Dogs to the line!
- They're starting.

326
00:28:05.039 --> 00:28:07.075
- Wish me luck.
- Luck?

327
00:28:07.140 --> 00:28:11.512
I don't wish you luck,
I wish you sense!

328
00:28:13.147 --> 00:28:15.216
Good luck, kiddo.

329
00:28:15.249 --> 00:28:17.318
Balto? What are you, nuts?

330
00:28:17.352 --> 00:28:20.955
If Steele catches you here,
he'll turn you into kibble!

331
00:28:20.988 --> 00:28:24.992
Let the half-dog run. It will be fun
making him eat our snow.

332
00:28:25.026 --> 00:28:27.028
Get set.

333
00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:30.031
- Balto?
- What does he think he's doing?

334
00:28:35.136 --> 00:28:37.605
Oh, Balto, come on, come on!

335
00:28:37.672 --> 00:28:40.041
Balto, go!

336
00:28:46.380 --> 00:28:48.349
Hey! That's a foul!

337
00:28:48.416 --> 00:28:51.786
Where's the referee? Is he blind?

338
00:28:54.956 --> 00:28:58.059
Go, Balto, go! Jump, jump, jump!

339
00:28:58.092 --> 00:29:00.862
Hey! That's my boy!

340
00:29:00.895 --> 00:29:02.897
Go, Balto!

341
00:29:05.800 --> 00:29:08.469
Balto, where are you going?

342
00:29:08.536 --> 00:29:13.041
That's the long way...
Balto, get back in the race!

343
00:29:19.480 --> 00:29:21.082
Sorry!

344
00:29:22.717 --> 00:29:25.420
Who's eating whose snow now, mutt?

345
00:29:28.990 --> 00:29:30.792
Time!

346
00:29:33.227 --> 00:29:36.931
Did I teach him well?.
I could kiss that crazy pooch.

347
00:29:43.938 --> 00:29:47.408
Ok, Nikki, Kaltag, Star, move it.
We're strapping up.

348
00:29:47.475 --> 00:29:50.011
Hey, now, just a second here, Steele.

349
00:29:50.078 --> 00:29:52.246
I was the fastest dog.

350
00:29:52.280 --> 00:29:55.850
You were the fastest... what?

351
00:29:55.917 --> 00:29:59.687
Do you honestly think any musher
would ever put you on his team?

352
00:29:59.754 --> 00:30:02.757
- You're more mixed-up thatn I thought!
- Steele!

353
00:30:02.790 --> 00:30:07.195
It doesn't matter who's on the team
as long as the medicine gets through.

354
00:30:07.260 --> 00:30:09.330
Stop being such a glory hound.

355
00:30:09.364 --> 00:30:12.700
You're a hundred per cent right,
Jenna. I... I...

356
00:30:12.800 --> 00:30:15.269
I wasn't thinking about those children.

357
00:30:15.303 --> 00:30:20.141
The important thing here is to get the medicine
through, and that's just what I wanna do.

358
00:30:20.174 --> 00:30:23.745
And when I come back I'm gonna
fold you five ways...

359
00:30:23.778 --> 00:30:26.314
and leave you for a cat toy.

360
00:30:26.347 --> 00:30:28.850
Good dog, Steele.

361
00:30:28.916 --> 00:30:32.353
Good boy! Now, let's take a look
at our winner here.

362
00:30:32.387 --> 00:30:35.990
Let's take a look at our winner.

363
00:30:38.426 --> 00:30:40.795
Ah, we can't trust this one.

364
00:30:40.828 --> 00:30:43.331
- He's part wolf.
- See those teeth?

365
00:30:43.364 --> 00:30:45.166
He might turn on me.

366
00:30:45.199 --> 00:30:48.536
Nikki, Kaltag, Star! Let's go!

367
00:30:56.477 --> 00:30:59.914
- Balto, I'm sorry...
- Better not talk to me, Jenna.

368
00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:03.551
- I might turn on you.
- Balto, wait. Balto!

369
00:31:08.456 --> 00:31:12.326
As long as there's hope
for those kids, I'll keep this lit.

370
00:31:12.360 --> 00:31:14.295
It'll guide the team back.

371
00:31:14.329 --> 00:31:17.398
Easy, easy. Back, back.

372
00:31:20.034 --> 00:31:23.204
The sooner they leave,
the sooner they're back.

373
00:31:23.237 --> 00:31:27.108
Stretch out, now.
Stretch out, Star.

374
00:32:13.855 --> 00:32:15.790
Easy with that.

375
00:32:17.058 --> 00:32:20.428
All right, now make sure
you lash her down tight.

376
00:32:20.460 --> 00:32:22.563
Giddap, Steele! Giddap!

377
00:32:22.597 --> 00:32:25.566
- Mush!
- Take care now, y'hear?

378
00:32:25.600 --> 00:32:29.570
- Good luck!
- Go on, boys, go on! Move along.

379
00:32:43.017 --> 00:32:44.819
Come on.

380
00:32:46.187 --> 00:32:47.822
Steele!

381
00:32:47.855 --> 00:32:51.659
Maybe we should go back. We're lost!

382
00:32:51.726 --> 00:32:55.196
I am not lost!

383
00:32:55.263 --> 00:32:57.765
Lost? Heh-heh. Did I say lost?

384
00:32:57.799 --> 00:32:59.634
You didn't let me finish.

385
00:32:59.667 --> 00:33:02.270
- I wanted to say... Aaah!
- This way!

386
00:33:17.819 --> 00:33:21.756
It's terrible, my friends.
Just terrible.

387
00:33:21.789 --> 00:33:25.793
Steele and his team... are lost.

388
00:33:25.827 --> 00:33:28.730
- No! Steele? - What
do you mean? - How come?

389
00:33:28.796 --> 00:33:31.499
- When?
- They missed the second checkpoint.

390
00:33:31.532 --> 00:33:33.735
They're off the trail.

391
00:33:33.800 --> 00:33:35.870
Can't they send another team?

392
00:33:35.903 --> 00:33:38.873
It's too dangerous
for us and our men.

393
00:33:38.906 --> 00:33:41.275
What about... them little ones?

394
00:33:41.309 --> 00:33:44.579
The medicine won't be here in time.

395
00:33:44.679 --> 00:33:47.181
We're going to lose them.

396
00:33:49.050 --> 00:33:51.386
Rosy.

397
00:33:55.356 --> 00:33:59.994
Please, Doctor,
it's the only medicine we got.

398
00:34:00.028 --> 00:34:02.296
ок.

399
00:34:19.614 --> 00:34:21.716
Jenna?

400
00:35:15.403 --> 00:35:16.904
Rosy.

401
00:35:21.809 --> 00:35:25.046
Balto, please.
Don't go crazy on me now.

402
00:35:26.848 --> 00:35:28.750
This is foolishness.

403
00:35:28.783 --> 00:35:32.020
You will die like a dog!
Oh, uh, no offence.

404
00:35:38.092 --> 00:35:41.029
You will be frozen stiff by morning!

405
00:35:42.964 --> 00:35:46.634
When you are big frozen-stiff
statue named Balto,

406
00:35:46.768 --> 00:35:48.936
don't come running to me!

407
00:35:50.938 --> 00:35:53.274
- He says...
- "Where is he going?"

408
00:35:53.307 --> 00:35:57.145
He's going into freezing coldness
to find a dog he doesn't like

409
00:35:57.178 --> 00:36:00.648
to bring medicine back to a town
that doesn't like him!

410
00:36:00.682 --> 00:36:03.584
Oh, no! I'm beginning
to understand the bear!

411
00:36:05.520 --> 00:36:07.855
Yes! Yes! Count us in!

412
00:36:07.955 --> 00:36:09.857
Bears! Dogs!

413
00:36:09.957 --> 00:36:12.727
Balto! Balto! Put me down!

414
00:36:16.964 --> 00:36:22.303
No brains at all! Might as well
be talking to hu... mans.

415
00:36:33.980 --> 00:36:36.884
So, let's go get the medicine.

416
00:36:36.918 --> 00:36:39.253
Wait a minute. Now you're coming?

417
00:36:39.320 --> 00:36:43.157
Spending days in bitter cold,
facing wild animals.

418
00:36:43.190 --> 00:36:45.326
risking death from exposure...

419
00:36:45.360 --> 00:36:48.696
.. is like holiday in old country.

420
00:36:50.832 --> 00:36:53.634
Oh! Great! We're goin' on holiday!

421
00:37:27.335 --> 00:37:29.370
Balto?

422
00:37:31.272 --> 00:37:33.541
Good, Balto!

423
00:37:33.574 --> 00:37:35.943
You took on the roughest, toughest.

424
00:37:35.943 --> 00:37:38.880
meanest tree in the forest...
and you won.

425
00:37:38.946 --> 00:37:41.382
I'm marking the trail.

426
00:37:41.416 --> 00:37:44.619
He's marking our trail.
He's very clever.

427
00:37:46.320 --> 00:37:49.757
And here I've been dropping bread crumbs!

428
00:37:52.760 --> 00:37:55.697
I spy with my little eye

429
00:37:55.730 --> 00:37:58.666
something beginning with "S".

430
00:38:15.116 --> 00:38:16.751
Steele.

431
00:38:24.659 --> 00:38:26.427
Bears!

432
00:38:27.895 --> 00:38:29.464
Come on.

433
00:38:30.630 --> 00:38:33.000
Steele and his team passed this way.

434
00:38:33.034 --> 00:38:35.136
Boy, is he lost.

435
00:38:43.610 --> 00:38:45.513
Steele!

436
00:38:45.546 --> 00:38:47.648
We're going in circles!

437
00:38:47.682 --> 00:38:49.550
- What?
- Gaa-aaah!

438
00:38:49.617 --> 00:38:54.389
Circles is a good thing. I mean,
they're, uh... They're circular.

439
00:38:55.990 --> 00:38:58.026
I know what I'm doing! It's...

440
00:39:00.128 --> 00:39:02.697
It's... this way! Come on!

441
00:39:47.275 --> 00:39:49.744
Ohh! I hit my head on somethin'.

442
00:39:49.777 --> 00:39:51.746
Yeah. My head.

443
00:39:51.779 --> 00:39:53.915
Looks like he's hurt bad, Steele.

444
00:39:53.948 --> 00:39:56.617
W- what are we gonna do now, Steele?

445
00:40:24.278 --> 00:40:27.615
Brilliant! Right on the beak!
What a bull's-eye!

446
00:40:30.118 --> 00:40:32.186
That did it! Who did that?

447
00:40:35.089 --> 00:40:38.326
I- It was him.

448
00:40:50.138 --> 00:40:52.140
Guys, I think...

449
00:40:55.910 --> 00:40:58.179
I think we should keep moving.

450
00:40:58.279 --> 00:41:01.482
Is that your answer to all problems?
Motion?

451
00:41:05.586 --> 00:41:07.922
Yeah, yeah! It's good.

452
00:41:07.955 --> 00:41:09.924
Come on! Let's get going.

453
00:41:09.957 --> 00:41:12.860
"Come on, boys. Let's go, boys.
Faster, boys. "

454
00:41:12.927 --> 00:41:15.296
Easy to say for a guy with four legs!

455
00:41:16.798 --> 00:41:19.801
OK, that's it.

456
00:41:19.867 --> 00:41:23.971
Is time for goose to
kick a little bear butt.

457
00:41:25.006 --> 00:41:27.175
Aha! Finally!

458
00:41:27.208 --> 00:41:31.379
Your old Uncle Boris
is making an impression!

459
00:41:31.446 --> 00:41:33.381
Now what?

460
00:42:27.335 --> 00:42:29.570
Jenna?

461
00:43:10.278 --> 00:43:13.247
Balto!

462
00:43:49.117 --> 00:43:52.320
Geronimo!

463
00:43:56.924 --> 00:43:58.860
Luk! Muk!

464
00:43:58.926 --> 00:44:00.895
They cannot swim!

465
00:44:00.928 --> 00:44:03.798
What? Polar bears who can't swim?

466
00:44:19.147 --> 00:44:20.915
He's drowning!

467
00:44:22.183 --> 00:44:23.618
No!

468
00:44:25.219 --> 00:44:27.155
Well?

469
00:44:27.255 --> 00:44:29.691
I don't see them.

470
00:44:32.727 --> 00:44:34.662
Where are they?

471
00:44:43.470 --> 00:44:45.306
- Balto!
- Muk! Luk!

472
00:44:46.808 --> 00:44:49.243
Balto!

473
00:44:58.386 --> 00:45:00.455
Come to life. Come to life.

474
00:45:00.488 --> 00:45:02.490
Breathe! Come on!

475
00:45:02.523 --> 00:45:05.827
Is he be OK? He's not breathing.
He doesn't look very well.

476
00:45:05.860 --> 00:45:07.895
Stop hitting him. Uncle Boris!

477
00:45:09.364 --> 00:45:13.000
Balto, I was so scared
I got people bumps.

478
00:45:15.403 --> 00:45:17.305
Boris...

479
00:45:18.439 --> 00:45:21.476
I know you think
this trip is crazy, but...

480
00:45:22.677 --> 00:45:24.545
I'm glad you came.

481
00:45:24.579 --> 00:45:28.516
Who else should you bring on a wild
goose chase but a goose, hmm?

482
00:45:28.549 --> 00:45:31.052
- Are you OK?
- Are you OK? Jen...

483
00:45:31.085 --> 00:45:35.656
I'm fine. Look, a message came through,
we have to take the mountain trail.

484
00:45:35.690 --> 00:45:39.127
But if we take Eagle Pass,
it'll save us half a day.

485
00:45:39.193 --> 00:45:43.464
It's blocked. The mountain trail
is dangerous, but we can do it.

486
00:45:43.530 --> 00:45:47.268
I'm beginning to see
there isn't anything you can't do.

487
00:45:47.335 --> 00:45:49.737
I'm seeing a few things too.

488
00:45:49.770 --> 00:45:52.006
and it's making the ice melt.

489
00:45:55.109 --> 00:45:57.745
I hate bears!

490
00:45:57.845 --> 00:46:01.582
You guys oughta learn how to swim someday.
You'd be very good at it.

491
00:46:05.086 --> 00:46:09.157
Of course we were in the water!
We were moving, we got wet...

492
00:46:10.792 --> 00:46:14.228
Luk! We were swimming!

493
00:46:17.265 --> 00:46:19.167
Ohh! Clumsy.

494
00:46:19.267 --> 00:46:22.437
- No, you're not. You're hurt.
- I'm fine.

495
00:46:26.808 --> 00:46:29.110
Maybe I'm not so fine.

496
00:46:29.143 --> 00:46:32.113
- You should all go ahead without me.
- Jenna...

497
00:46:32.146 --> 00:46:36.351
I'll be slowing everyone down.
Rosy can't hold out much longer.

498
00:46:38.686 --> 00:46:42.824
Muk, you and Luk carry
Jenna back to town on this.

499
00:46:42.857 --> 00:46:47.695
And this time don't take time out for a swim!

500
00:46:47.762 --> 00:46:49.831
You can make sure of that, Boris.

501
00:46:49.864 --> 00:46:53.267
You're gonna lead them home.
Just follow my marks.

502
00:46:53.300 --> 00:46:56.537
- You're going alone?
- Won't be the first time.

503
00:46:56.604 --> 00:47:00.208
Here. Afraid it won't keep you very warm.

504
00:47:00.274 --> 00:47:02.810
Yeah, it will.

505
00:47:07.715 --> 00:47:11.152
Well, of course Balto will come back.

506
00:47:11.185 --> 00:47:13.821
He's Balto, will he?

507
00:47:13.855 --> 00:47:16.991
Hey! I'm coming back
with the medicine.

508
00:47:17.025 --> 00:47:18.793
I promise, Jenna.

509
00:47:18.826 --> 00:47:21.129
Go ahead, guys. Take her home.

510
00:47:21.162 --> 00:47:24.699
Balto, I do not like
leaving you out here alone.

511
00:47:24.766 --> 00:47:27.935
Who's going to tell you
how cold you are?

512
00:47:27.969 --> 00:47:30.071
Boris.

513
00:47:30.138 --> 00:47:32.340
They need you even more than I do.

514
00:47:36.677 --> 00:47:39.647
Let me tell you something, Balto.

515
00:47:39.680 --> 00:47:43.051
A dog cannot make this journey alone.

516
00:47:44.419 --> 00:47:48.556
But maybe a wolf can.

517
00:47:50.692 --> 00:47:53.594
Right, you two balls of fluff! Let's move!

518
00:47:53.660 --> 00:47:55.897
Hey! Two, three, four!

519
00:47:55.930 --> 00:47:58.666
<i>Nome. Stop.</i>

520
00:47:58.700 --> 00:48:03.104
<i>Cannot send more antitoxin. Stop.</i>

521
00:48:03.170 --> 00:48:07.375
<i>Weather too severe. Stop.</i>

522
00:48:07.408 --> 00:48:11.279
<i>Lost sled team only hope. Stop.</i>

523
00:48:11.345 --> 00:48:14.882
<i>Our prayers are with them.</i>

524
00:48:14.916 --> 00:48:17.418
<i>Anchorage. Stop.</i>

525
00:48:44.912 --> 00:48:46.614
Steele.

526
00:48:55.990 --> 00:48:57.892
Oh!

527
00:49:00.595 --> 00:49:02.330
Balto!

528
00:49:02.397 --> 00:49:04.932
- Is that Balto?
- How did you find us?

529
00:49:04.999 --> 00:49:10.004
- Is anyone hurt?
- Everyone... is... fine.

530
00:49:10.070 --> 00:49:14.308
Yeah, but our mushier hit his head
and he didn't get up.

531
00:49:14.375 --> 00:49:17.445
- And he's not movin'.
- All right, follow me.

532
00:49:17.478 --> 00:49:19.280
I can lead you home.

533
00:49:19.414 --> 00:49:22.350
We don't need your help!

534
00:49:22.450 --> 00:49:24.652
М- maybe we should listen to him.

535
00:49:26.654 --> 00:49:28.589
How would youse get us home?

536
00:49:28.656 --> 00:49:32.026
Well, I marked the trail, like this.

537
00:49:32.093 --> 00:49:33.961
- Oh! Yeah!
- Ohh!

538
00:49:33.995 --> 00:49:38.066
I'll get us back.
I'm the lead dog. I'm in charge.

539
00:49:38.099 --> 00:49:42.036
Then let me take back the medicine.
They're getting sicker.

540
00:49:45.039 --> 00:49:49.310
Touch that box
and I'll tear you apart.

541
00:49:49.344 --> 00:49:52.347
- Two bones says Steele takes him.
- You're on.

542
00:49:54.615 --> 00:49:57.952
Steele, I'm not leaving
without that medicine.

543
00:49:59.387 --> 00:50:02.357
Who do you think you are?

544
00:50:02.390 --> 00:50:04.659
Hey, this is gonna be good.

545
00:50:04.692 --> 00:50:09.464
Since... Since when do you need
a pedigree to help someone?

546
00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:13.167
Steele.

547
00:50:13.200 --> 00:50:15.436
Let me help you.

548
00:50:15.503 --> 00:50:17.472
Look at his eyes!

549
00:50:25.246 --> 00:50:28.516
- He'll feel that tomorrow.
- I think he is feeling it now!

550
00:50:28.649 --> 00:50:30.318
Ouch!

551
00:50:32.353 --> 00:50:34.555
I don't want to fight.

552
00:50:40.160 --> 00:50:42.930
- Whoa! That can't be legal!
- Yeah!

553
00:50:50.938 --> 00:50:52.740
That stuff is fragile!

554
00:50:52.774 --> 00:50:55.710
What's with Steele?
All Balto wants to do is help.

555
00:51:12.427 --> 00:51:14.862
Ah! Look!

556
00:51:50.264 --> 00:51:53.568
Oh, good boy.

557
00:52:14.322 --> 00:52:16.257
Mush!

558
00:52:19.527 --> 00:52:22.964
Go ahead, wolf-dog!
You'll never get home!

559
00:52:24.165 --> 00:52:26.968
I'll make sure of that.

560
00:52:28.670 --> 00:52:30.705
I'll show 'em.

561
00:52:30.838 --> 00:52:34.208
Why not this way?
How about over here?

562
00:52:35.276 --> 00:52:37.979
Oops! Wrong way!

563
00:52:40.715 --> 00:52:42.517
Oh, no.

564
00:52:46.854 --> 00:52:48.690
Which way, Balto, which way?

565
00:52:48.756 --> 00:52:51.659
- Which way?
- Uh, this way.

566
00:53:10.144 --> 00:53:14.248
- Why are you taking us in circles?
- I'm not!

567
00:53:14.315 --> 00:53:18.219
I mean, I don't know. It's Steele.

568
00:53:18.286 --> 00:53:21.255
Maybe we was
better off with him there.

569
00:53:21.322 --> 00:53:23.324
No! Come on. Mush!

570
00:53:30.330 --> 00:53:33.167
Balto, slow down! Wait... Uhh!

571
00:53:36.270 --> 00:53:39.207
Hey! Hey! Goin' too fast!

572
00:53:57.725 --> 00:53:59.260
Look out!

573
00:54:04.599 --> 00:54:06.701
All right!

574
00:54:06.734 --> 00:54:10.238
Good catch, Balto!

575
00:54:24.952 --> 00:54:26.454
I don't get it.

576
00:54:26.487 --> 00:54:29.824
how could Balto hope to
find Steele and his team?

577
00:54:29.924 --> 00:54:31.826
They were off the trail.

578
00:54:31.893 --> 00:54:34.062
Well, he's... tracking them.

579
00:54:34.095 --> 00:54:36.064
That mutt?

580
00:54:36.097 --> 00:54:39.467
Tracking a championship team
in a blizzard?

581
00:54:46.307 --> 00:54:49.143
- Balto?
- Steele!

582
00:54:49.177 --> 00:54:52.046
- You're alive!
- You're back!

583
00:54:52.080 --> 00:54:55.850
- Where ya been?
- Are ya OK?

584
00:54:55.917 --> 00:54:58.186
Steele, w-where are the others?

585
00:54:58.252 --> 00:55:03.458
- What happened to you?
- Well, one by one they... fell.

586
00:55:03.524 --> 00:55:06.194
Frozen, barely alive.

587
00:55:09.930 --> 00:55:12.700
I pulled four onto the sled.

588
00:55:12.767 --> 00:55:15.636
Three more on my back!

589
00:55:17.705 --> 00:55:20.575
And, uh, I walked...

590
00:55:20.608 --> 00:55:22.543
and I walked.

591
00:55:22.610 --> 00:55:25.546
but i-it was just...
it was too late.

592
00:55:25.613 --> 00:55:27.615
They were...

593
00:55:27.648 --> 00:55:30.618
What about the medicine?

594
00:55:30.650 --> 00:55:33.054
Well, uh, I... I went on,

595
00:55:33.154 --> 00:55:35.823
d- dragging the medicine alone...

596
00:55:35.857 --> 00:55:37.492
all alone...

597
00:55:37.525 --> 00:55:39.560
and... and then suddenly...

598
00:55:40.862 --> 00:55:43.831
that wolf-dog appeared, Balto.

599
00:55:43.865 --> 00:55:47.201
H- he demanded I let him
take the medicine.

600
00:55:48.636 --> 00:55:53.574
You know, he just wanted
so much to be a hero in your eyes.

601
00:55:53.640 --> 00:55:56.644
And h-he grabbed the crate.

602
00:55:58.312 --> 00:56:00.648
but he couldn't handle it.

603
00:56:00.715 --> 00:56:03.217
H- he couldn't see the patch of ice...

604
00:56:03.250 --> 00:56:05.920
Th-the snow, the wind and...

605
00:56:05.987 --> 00:56:08.456
And then the log and the cliff...

606
00:56:08.489 --> 00:56:11.225
Well, he just didn't have a ch...

607
00:56:11.259 --> 00:56:12.694
He just...

608
00:56:12.760 --> 00:56:15.663
I'm sorry.

609
00:56:15.797 --> 00:56:17.665
And then...

610
00:56:20.068 --> 00:56:22.603
My bandana!

611
00:56:22.670 --> 00:56:27.075
He... made me promise
to take care of you, Jenna.

612
00:56:32.413 --> 00:56:34.382
You're lying.

613
00:56:34.415 --> 00:56:37.852
Steele's lying.

614
00:56:37.885 --> 00:56:39.854
Balto's alive.

615
00:56:39.887 --> 00:56:42.757
And he's coming home.

616
00:56:44.025 --> 00:56:48.730
Uh... Well, you know,
she needs a little time.

617
00:57:28.302 --> 00:57:32.006
The sun. Ice caps.

618
00:57:45.820 --> 00:57:47.588
Balto.

619
00:57:59.834 --> 00:58:01.536
Rosy.

620
00:58:37.472 --> 00:58:39.007
Hmm?

621
00:58:51.652 --> 00:58:54.022
<i>Let me tell you something, Balto.</i>

622
00:58:54.055 --> 00:58:58.693
<i>A dog cannot make this journey alone.</i>

623
00:58:58.760 --> 00:59:02.764
<i>But maybe a wolf can.</i>

624
00:59:48.743 --> 00:59:51.879
Great, things are not bad enough.
Now we got wolves.

625
00:59:51.913 --> 00:59:54.382
Wolves?

626
00:59:54.415 --> 00:59:57.719
- Hey, over here!
- What is it? What?

627
00:59:57.752 --> 01:00:01.089
- Balto?
- And he's got the medicine!

628
01:00:01.122 --> 01:00:04.025
Come on, Balto. Youse can make it.

629
01:00:07.762 --> 01:00:10.732
That's the most amazing, the most fantastic,
that is the most incredible...

630
01:00:10.765 --> 01:00:13.601
That's the most phenomenal...

631
01:00:13.634 --> 01:00:16.004
That's good! Ohh!

632
01:00:16.070 --> 01:00:19.974
Hey, he has got the feet of a wolf there.

633
01:00:20.074 --> 01:00:23.177
- Come on, Balto.
- Keep tryin', baby.

634
01:00:23.277 --> 01:00:26.581
- Pull! Pull! You got it!
- Just keep pullin'!

635
01:00:26.614 --> 01:00:29.851
- You're almost there.
- Yeah! You got it!

636
01:00:29.917 --> 01:00:33.321
- Come on, Balto!
- Come on, let's go!

637
01:00:33.454 --> 01:00:36.924
- Let's go!
- Yes! You're there!

638
01:00:36.958 --> 01:00:40.194
- That's it, that's it!
- All right!

639
01:00:40.260 --> 01:00:43.197
-Yeah! All right!
- You did it!

640
01:00:43.264 --> 01:00:45.433
Congratulations! That was great!

641
01:01:43.390 --> 01:01:45.693
Come on! Mush!

642
01:02:20.528 --> 01:02:22.230
Gesundheit.

643
01:04:18.646 --> 01:04:21.215
Mush!

644
01:05:04.692 --> 01:05:06.461
Oh, dear.

645
01:05:07.895 --> 01:05:10.531
Come back to bed.

646
01:05:13.900 --> 01:05:16.304
Here, drink this.

647
01:05:18.873 --> 01:05:20.808
Thanks.

648
01:05:38.426 --> 01:05:40.395
Balto.

649
01:05:45.600 --> 01:05:47.669
В- B-Balto.

650
01:05:56.844 --> 01:05:58.446
Balto.

651
01:06:01.149 --> 01:06:03.418
Balto's back!

652
01:06:08.823 --> 01:06:10.358
Jenna.

653
01:06:20.335 --> 01:06:22.303
The team!

654
01:06:22.337 --> 01:06:24.505
They made it!

655
01:06:48.229 --> 01:06:50.164
Of course, as you know.

656
01:06:50.264 --> 01:06:52.367
I swam and I swam.

657
01:06:52.400 --> 01:06:54.736
I was freezing cold. And then...

658
01:06:56.904 --> 01:06:59.741
Finally, I said, Steele,

659
01:06:59.807 --> 01:07:02.810
you'll have to gnaw
your way to the surface.

660
01:07:02.844 --> 01:07:05.213
So I... What?

661
01:07:05.246 --> 01:07:08.249
It's Balto. With the medicine!

662
01:07:10.918 --> 01:07:13.488
Steele, you are positively...

663
01:07:13.554 --> 01:07:16.190
disposable!

664
01:07:23.730 --> 01:07:25.466
OK, OK. I can explain.

665
01:07:25.500 --> 01:07:27.435
Tell me about it.

666
01:07:27.502 --> 01:07:29.437
You guys weren't there, so you don't...

667
01:07:29.504 --> 01:07:32.940
Wait a minute, guys.
Wait just a second. Please?

668
01:07:33.007 --> 01:07:34.175
Get lost.

669
01:07:56.464 --> 01:08:00.234
Steady, there. Easy, now.
That's had a long journey.

670
01:08:00.268 --> 01:08:02.337
- How is he?
- He's gonna be OK.

671
01:08:20.922 --> 01:08:23.424
Good dog, Balto.

672
01:08:23.458 --> 01:08:24.959
Dear, dear Balto.

673
01:08:26.060 --> 01:08:28.396
Good boy!

674
01:08:28.429 --> 01:08:31.366
Not dog! Not wolf!

675
01:08:31.399 --> 01:08:33.901
You're a hero!

676
01:08:33.935 --> 01:08:36.671
Balto!

677
01:08:44.178 --> 01:08:47.615
Come on, boy.
There's someone wants to see you.

678
01:08:47.715 --> 01:08:49.617
Thank you! Thank you!

679
01:09:04.465 --> 01:09:06.267
Mommy?

680
01:09:06.300 --> 01:09:08.236
Rosy, darling. Ohh!

681
01:09:08.269 --> 01:09:10.938
- I fell asleep.
- Rosy.

682
01:09:14.876 --> 01:09:17.111
It's such a relief.

683
01:09:25.186 --> 01:09:26.688
Balto.

684
01:09:27.755 --> 01:09:29.791
I'd be lost without you.

685
01:09:38.132 --> 01:09:39.801
Jenna.

686
01:10:00.755 --> 01:10:02.924
Way to go, Balto!

687
01:10:02.990 --> 01:10:06.227
He has the most endurance, the most fidelity,
the most intelligence!

688
01:10:06.260 --> 01:10:08.796
They should build a statue of him!

689
01:10:08.863 --> 01:10:11.666
- You said it!
- I did?

690
01:10:37.959 --> 01:10:40.895
This is it. Grandma.
Blaze found it.

691
01:10:49.103 --> 01:10:51.406
What does it say?

692
01:10:51.439 --> 01:10:55.610
"Dedicated to the... " Indomable?

693
01:10:55.677 --> 01:10:57.578
Indomitable.

694
01:10:57.645 --> 01:11:02.583
"Indomitable spirit
of the sled dogs... "

695
01:11:02.617 --> 01:11:05.586
"... that relayed antitoxin

696
01:11:05.620 --> 01:11:11.159
"600 miles from Nenana
to the relief of stricken Nome...

697
01:11:11.259 --> 01:11:14.329
"in the winter of 1925. "

698
01:11:14.395 --> 01:11:18.466
"Endurance, fidelity, intelligence. "

699
01:11:18.499 --> 01:11:21.436
Balto really did do all of that,
didn't he, Grandma?

700
01:11:21.469 --> 01:11:23.771
Oh, yes, sweetheart, he really did.

701
01:11:23.805 --> 01:11:26.574
And today they run
the Iditarod Dog Race

702
01:11:26.607 --> 01:11:29.610
over the very path
he and the others took.

703
01:11:29.644 --> 01:11:33.448
- Can Blaze do that too. Grandma?
- Maybe.

704
01:11:33.480 --> 01:11:35.616
With practice.

705
01:11:36.918 --> 01:11:39.921
A lot of practice.

706
01:11:39.954 --> 01:11:42.490
Come on, Blaze. Come on! Mush!

707
01:11:49.764 --> 01:11:51.866
Thank you, Balto.

708
01:11:51.933 --> 01:11:54.936
I would've been lost without you.

709
01:11:58.006 --> 01:11:59.941
Grandma Rosy!

710
01:12:04.812 --> 01:12:07.015
Grandma Rosy, come on!
